and Petersen illuminate the key values and questions that should be driving this conversation: trust, fairness, flexibility, inclusive workplaces, equity, and work-life balance. Above all, they argue that companies need to listen to their employees - and that this will promote, rather than impede, productivity and profitability. Working from home is about so much more than zoom meetings and hybrid schedules: it aims to reshape our entire relationship to the office.  -- adapted from Amazon info"}],"tableOfContents":"Flexibility -- Culture -- Technologies of the office -- Community -- A final note to bosses -- Letters to workers.","targetAudience":{"@authority":"marctarget","#text":"adult"},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Charlie Warzel and Anne Helen Petersen."},"\"This is a Borzoi Book\"--Title page verso.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references."}],"subject":[{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Telecommuting"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Flexible work arrangements"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Industrial relations"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Conditions de travail flexibles"},{"@authority":"rvm","topic":"Relations industrielles"},{"@authority":"aat","topic":"industrial relations"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"SELF-HELP / Personal Growth / Success"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"BUSINESS & ECONOMICS / Careers / General"},{"@authority":"bisacsh","topic":"BUSINESS & ECONOMICS / Workplace Culture"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Flexible work arrangements"},{"@authority":"fast","topic":"Telecommuting"},{"@authority":"sears","topic":"Telecommuting"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HD2336.3 .W37 2021"},{"@edition":"23","@authority":"ddc","#text":"658.3/123"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780593320099"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0593320093"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780593314449"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0593314441"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9781524712105"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"152